## 2026-08-09 - US-017 (security-audit.md L4)

Custom proposals now require an UpdatePath.

- `needsUpdatePath` in `applyProposals` (`src/client-state.ts`) now also
  turns true when any proposal in the commit has a numeric (custom)
  proposal type. RFC 9420 12.4 only exempts add, psk and reinit, so a
  custom-only commit was previously accepted with no path and an all-zero
  commit secret -- a state change with no forward secrecy or PCS.
- New test `test/scenario/custom-proposal-update-path.ts`, registered in
  `test/matrix.ts`. It covers the flag itself, the sending side
  (`createCommit` emits a path for a custom-only commit) and the
  receiving side (a forged pathless custom-only commit is rejected with
  `Update path is required`), plus a sanity pass on the well-formed
  commit.
- Files changed: `src/client-state.ts`, `test/matrix.ts`,
  `test/scenario/custom-proposal-update-path.ts`, `specs/prd.json`,
  `progress.log`.

- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `grouped` in `applyProposals` deliberately drops custom proposals
    (they are never applied to the tree), so any rule that must see them
    has to read `allProposals` instead. `needsUpdatePath` was reading
    only `grouped`, which is exactly how L4 slipped in.
  - `process-messages.ts` checks `needsUpdatePath` *before* verifying the
    confirmation tag, so a forged pathless commit in a test fails with
    `ValidationError('Update path is required')` rather than
    `CryptoVerificationError`. A fake confirmation tag is fine in such a
    test; assert on the message with a `RegExp` to keep the two apart.
  - `test/scenario/require-update-path.ts` is the template for
    "forge a pathless commit and expect rejection": build it with
    `createContentCommitSignature` + `createConfirmationTag` +
    `protectPublicMessage`, then feed it to `processPublicMessage`.
  - The existing `test/scenario/custom-proposal.ts` needed no change --
    it commits the custom proposal through `createCommit`, which already
    honours `needsUpdatePath`.
  - Full suite: 45145 tests, 45144 pass, 1 fail -- still the same
    pre-existing, unrelated `test/example/how-to-use.ts` "should render
    an item for each step". `npx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` and
    `npm run lint` both exit 0.
