## 2026-08-09 - US-021 (security-audit L10)

Two remote-triggerable errors given the right shape: a protocol-version
check on the Welcome join path, and a `ValidationError` instead of an
`InternalError` when a Remove would empty the ratchet tree.

- `joinGroup` (`src/client-state.ts`) now rejects a Welcome whose
  GroupInfo `groupContext.version` differs from the joiner's own
  `keyPackage.version`, alongside the existing cipher-suite check. The
  committer is supposed to catch this in `validateKeyPackage`, but the
  joiner cannot assume the committer is honest.
- `condenseRatchetTreeAfterRemove` (`src/ratchet-tree.ts`) throws
  `ValidationError('Cannot remove the only remaining leaf of a group')`
  when `stripBlankNodes` leaves nothing. Previously the empty array fell
  through to `extendRatchetTree`, whose `tree[-1] === undefined` guard
  threw `InternalError` -- a library-bug signal for something a peer can
  ask for.
- New tests in `test/validation/version-and-last-leaf.ts`, registered in
  `test/matrix.ts`. Both fail on the pre-fix tree (verified by stashing
  the two source files and re-running).

Files changed: `src/client-state.ts`, `src/ratchet-tree.ts`,
`test/validation/version-and-last-leaf.ts`, `test/matrix.ts`,
`AGENTS.md`, `progress.log`, `specs/prd.json`.

- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The reachable path for the empty-tree remove is
    `joinGroupExternal(..., resync = true)` against a single-member
    group: it calls `removeLeafNode` on the sole leaf *before* adding the
    joiner's new leaf. `applyProposals` reaches the same code, but a
    commit cannot get there -- a committer may not remove itself, so in a
    one-member group there is no other leaf to target.
  - Resync matching goes through
    `clientConfig.keyPackageEqualityConfig.compareKeyPackageToLeafNode`,
    which by default compares signature public keys. Reusing a signature
    key across key packages only works on Ed25519
    (`generateKeyPackage`'s `signatureKeyPair` option throws otherwise),
    so a matrix test that needs a resync supplies its own equality config
    comparing credential identity instead.
  - Asserting only `err instanceof ValidationError` on a join-path test
    is nearly worthless: `joinGroup` has a dozen `ValidationError` exits,
    and this test first passed for the wrong reason ("Could not find own
    leaf when processing welcome" fires later in the same function). The
    assertion has to pin the specific error.
  - Full suite: 45307 tests, 45306 pass, 1 fail -- still the same
    pre-existing, unrelated `test/example/how-to-use.ts` "should render
    an item for each step". Both typechecks exit 0 and `npm run lint`
    exits 0.
