## 2026-08-09 - US-023
- Security headers on the realistic demo Worker. `securityHeaders(origin)`
  is a new pure rule in `example-realistic-demo/room-logic.ts` returning
  `Content-Security-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and
  `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`. The CSP is `default-src 'none'` with
  `'self'` for script, style, img, font and connect, `'none'` for
  base-uri, form-action and frame-ancestors, plus the request origin's
  own socket source (`ws://localhost:8787`, `wss://<host>` in
  production) named explicitly in `connect-src`.
- `index.ts`: the default export's `fetch` now calls a new `route`
  function and puts the headers on whatever it returns, so there is one
  exit from the Worker. A 101 is passed through untouched. Responses from
  the ASSETS binding and from the Durable Object have immutable headers,
  so the wrapper rebuilds with `new Response(res.body, res)`.
- `wrangler.jsonc`: `run_worker_first` is now `true` (was `["/api/*"]`)
  and the assets binding is named `ASSETS`, so the Worker serves the
  client and can put the headers on the SPA shell and every asset.
  `worker-configuration.d.ts` regenerated.
- Files: `example-realistic-demo/room-logic.ts`,
  `example-realistic-demo/index.ts`,
  `example-realistic-demo/wrangler.jsonc`,
  `example-realistic-demo/worker-configuration.d.ts`,
  `example-realistic-demo/AGENTS.md`,
  `test/example-realistic-demo/room-logic.ts`, `specs/prd.json`.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Static assets do not reach the Worker unless `run_worker_first` is
    `true`. With the previous `["/api/*"]`, headers set in the Worker
    appear on API replies and on nothing else, which curls green on
    `/api/health` and fails the actual criterion.
  - A response handed back by `env.ASSETS.fetch` or by a Durable Object
    stub has immutable headers. `headers.set` on it throws at runtime,
    not at typecheck; rebuild with `new Response(res.body, res)`.
  - Verification used here, in order: `npm run build:realistic`, then
    `npx wrangler dev -c example-realistic-demo/wrangler.jsonc --port
    8787` in the background, then curl the shell, an asset and
    `/api/health`, then `node example-realistic-demo/scripts/probe.mjs`
    (26/26, exit 0), then a real browser load of :8787 -- a CSP violation
    shows up only there, since the Node suite and the probe never parse
    the header. Zero console messages after creating a room, which also
    proves the socket source is right. Stopped with
    `pkill -f "wrangler dev -c example-realistic-demo"`, confirmed with
    `pgrep -fl example-realistic-demo` (no match).
  - Full suite: 45321 tests, 45320 pass, 1 fail -- still the same
    pre-existing, unrelated `test/example/how-to-use.ts` "should render
    an item for each step". `npm run lint`, `npx tsc -p tsconfig.json
    --noEmit` and `npx tsc -p example-realistic-demo/tsconfig.json
    --noEmit` all exit 0 with no errors.
