Worker stopped by repo path with pkill on
`/Users/nick/code/webcrypto-mls/node_modules`, confirmed with `pgrep -fl
"/Users/nick/code/webcrypto-mls"` (no match).

- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - A failure carried forward as "pre-existing and unrelated" is a claim
    that decays. This one was quoted verbatim through twenty-three
    stories and was a two-line fix in the file it pointed at the whole
    time. Read the failure once before inheriting the label.
  - A fenced code block inside a markdown bullet has to be indented to
    the bullet's text column. At column 0 it terminates the list, and
    the damage is invisible in a diff and invisible in an editor -- it
    shows up only rendered. The README's Security Considerations section
    is almost entirely bullets with examples under them.
  - Verifying a demo build means grepping the built asset, not reading
    the source gate. `import.meta.env.DEV` is replaced with a literal
    `false` and the block is dropped; a `MODE` comparison is not, and
    `npm run build-example` runs `--mode staging`.
  - The order that keeps a >10 minute `npm test` from being the thing
    that runs out the clock: start it in the background against a tree
    already linted and typechecked, review while it runs, then re-run at
    the end only if the review changed behavior. Comment and markdown
    edits do not need a second run; this session did one anyway, because
    the full suite is this story's gate.
  - A heredoc containing backticks and apostrophes can be rewritten
    before the shell sees it. Write the text to a file with the file
    tool and `cat` that onto `progress.log` instead.
